552	418	508	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Percentage-based log growth is dangerous on large databases: a 100GB log with 10% growth = 10GB growth event. Each growth event: (1) zeroes out new space (instant file initialization does NOT apply to log files), (2) blocks all log writes during growth, (3) can cause application timeouts. Example: 50GB log, 10% growth -> 5GB growth -> 30-60 seconds on SSD, minutes on HDD. Fix: ALTER DATABASE MODIFY FILE (NAME = logfile, FILEGROWTH = 512MB) -- use fixed size increments of 256MB-1GB depending on workload. Pre-size logs to expected maximum to avoid runtime growth entirely.
