660	465	615	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	SQL Server RLS (Row-Level Security) applies filter and block predicates to all queries including those executed by replication agents. If the Distribution Agent runs under a security context that the RLS filter predicate does not whitelist, replicated INSERT/UPDATE operations may be silently filtered (filter predicate) or blocked with an error (block predicate). This is particularly insidious because filter predicates cause silent data loss — rows are applied but immediately invisible. Fix: add exemption for the replication agent's execution context in the RLS predicate function using IS_MEMBER('db_owner') or SUSER_SNAME() checks, or disable RLS during replication with ALTER SECURITY POLICY ... WITH (STATE = OFF).
