670	469	625	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	SQL Server peer-to-peer transactional replication (Enterprise Edition) propagates changes from each node to all other nodes asynchronously. Transaction ordering is NOT guaranteed — if Node A and Node B both update the same row within the propagation window, the final state may differ across nodes. Peer-to-peer conflict detection (added in SQL Server 2008) detects these but does not automatically resolve them — it requires manual intervention or a custom resolver. Error 22815 = conflict detected on peer. The fundamental design assumes non-overlapping writes — partitioned by originator_id. Fix: partition writes by node, enable conflict detection, implement application-level serialization.
