673	470	628	1	next	\N	next	\N	Network partitions in SQL Server multi-master topologies (peer-to-peer transactional or merge replication) cause split-brain scenarios where isolated nodes continue accepting writes independently. Upon reconnection: (1) peer-to-peer replication may detect conflicts for overlapping writes, (2) merge replication resolves conflicts per article-level resolver but silent data loss occurs for the losing side, (3) the distribution database may grow very large holding undelivered commands during the partition. Unlike AG with automatic failover, replication topologies have no quorum mechanism — all nodes continue operating independently. Fix: monitor distribution agent latency, configure alerts for agent inactivity, use sp_replmonitorsubscriptionpendingcmds to track command backlogs.
