1174	711	1123	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Unselective queries are a major source of buffer pool pressure because they bring large numbers of pages into the cache that may never be reused, evicting hot pages in the process. The reads_per_row ratio is a key metric: a well-indexed point lookup should read 2-4 pages per row, while a full scan reads thousands. Common causes: missing WHERE clauses, LIKE '%pattern%' leading wildcards, functions on columns preventing index seeks, implicit conversions. Fix: add appropriate indexes, rewrite queries to be more selective, use query hints (OPTIMIZE FOR) for parameterized queries with skewed distributions, or use indexed views for complex aggregations.
