1180	714	1129	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Concurrent workload contention on the buffer pool manifests as PAGELATCH waits (in-memory page access contention) and Free list stalls (no free pages available in the buffer pool). Classic scenarios: (1) last-page insert contention on identity columns (PAGELATCH_EX on allocation pages), (2) tempdb contention from many concurrent queries using temp tables, (3) hot pages in lookup tables accessed by every transaction. Free list stalls/sec > 0 means the lazywriter cannot free pages fast enough for demand. Fix: increase buffer pool memory, reduce concurrent scan-heavy workloads, use hash partitioning for insert-heavy tables, move tempdb to faster storage, optimize queries to touch fewer pages per execution.
