1182	715	1131	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Hot page concentration occurs when many concurrent operations need exclusive or update access to the same buffer pool page. The most common hot spots: (1) tempdb PFS/GAM/SGAM pages when many sessions create/drop temp tables simultaneously, (2) the last page of a clustered index on an identity/sequence column (last-page insert contention), (3) frequently updated lookup/counter tables. In tempdb, page_id 1 is the first PFS page, 2 is the first GAM, 3 is the first SGAM. SQL Server 2016+ has tempdb metadata optimization. Fix: (1) for tempdb, add multiple data files (1 per logical CPU up to 8), enable trace flag 1118 (uniform extent allocation, default in 2016+), (2) for identity inserts, use GUID keys or hash partitioning, (3) for counter tables, use separate rows per partition.
