1184	716	1133	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Missing indexes are the most common and most fixable cause of buffer pool pressure. sys.dm_db_missing_index_* DMVs accumulate missing index suggestions from the query optimizer during normal query compilation. The improvement_measure formula (avg_user_impact * (user_seeks + user_scans) * avg_total_user_cost) prioritizes indexes with the highest overall benefit. Important caveats: (1) these are suggestions, not commands -- always test before creating, (2) too many indexes increase write overhead and buffer pool pressure for modifications, (3) consider covering indexes (with INCLUDE columns) to eliminate key lookups, (4) consolidate overlapping suggestions. Fix: create the top 5-10 missing indexes by improvement_measure, verify query performance improves, and monitor for index usage with sys.dm_db_index_usage_stats.
