1200	724	1149	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	When a query references objects without schema qualification (e.g., SELECT * FROM Orders instead of SELECT * FROM dbo.Orders), SQL Server creates a separate plan cache entry for each user_id because the unqualified name resolves differently depending on the user's default schema. Even if all users ultimately resolve to dbo.Orders, the engine caches per-user because it cannot prove equivalence at cache time. The plan_attributes DMV shows user_id as a cache key. Fix: (1) always use two-part object names (schema.table) in all queries and stored procedures, (2) set all application logins to default schema = dbo, (3) use stored procedures which cache independently of user context, (4) code review application SQL for unqualified references.
