1230	739	1178	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	AG replication lag has two components: (1) log_send_queue: log not yet sent to secondary (network/bandwidth bottleneck), (2) redo_queue: log sent but not yet replayed on secondary (I/O or CPU bottleneck on secondary). For synchronous replicas, log_send_queue should be near 0 (log is hardened before commit). For asynchronous replicas, some lag is expected but should be bounded. Causes: slow network, I/O contention on secondary, long-running queries on readable secondary blocking redo, CPU saturation. Fix: (1) address I/O bottleneck on secondary, (2) increase network bandwidth, (3) kill long queries on secondary, (4) add parallel redo (SQL 2016+ automatic for databases > 100GB).
