1295	767	1243	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Idle-in-transaction sessions are a major cause of connection pool exhaustion. The application begins a transaction (e.g., BEGIN TRAN), performs some work, then waits for user input, calls an external API, or encounters application-level processing without committing/rolling back. The connection cannot be returned to the pool because the transaction is still open. This also blocks other sessions if locks are held. Detection key: status = 'sleeping' with an active transaction. Fix: (1) set transaction timeout in the application, (2) use TransactionScope with timeout in .NET, (3) implement connection abort for idle-in-transaction sessions via Resource Governor or a monitoring job, (4) redesign application to use short transactions (open, do work, commit immediately), (5) set query_wait_s in Resource Governor workload group.
