1382	806	1330	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Connection storms are a cascading failure pattern: (1) server reaches worker thread limit, (2) new connections time out, (3) application pools mark connections as failed, (4) all pool instances simultaneously try to recreate their connections, (5) the burst of connection attempts further overwhelms the server. This is especially severe with microservices where dozens of instances each maintain a pool. Fix: implement exponential backoff with jitter in connection retry logic, use circuit breaker patterns to stop retrying during outages, reduce pool max sizes across applications, and consider Resource Governor to limit per-workload connections. Emergency: sp_configure 'max worker threads' increase (requires restart) or killing idle sessions.
