1394	810	1342	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Transactional replication uses three types of agents, each requiring dedicated connections: (1) Log Reader Agent — reads transaction log and writes to distribution DB (2 connections per published DB), (2) Distribution Agent — moves commands from distribution DB to subscribers (1-2 connections per subscription), (3) Snapshot Agent — generates initial data snapshots (active only during snapshot generation). A server with 10 published databases and 5 subscribers could have 30+ persistent replication connections. AG replicas use dedicated mirroring endpoints (port 5022 by default) and do not consume user connection slots. Fix: consolidate publications where possible, move the distribution database to a separate server, use push subscriptions instead of pull to centralize agent connections, and monitor replication agent connection count as part of capacity planning.
