1448	830	1396	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Parallel hash join distributes rows across threads using a hash function on the join key. If the key has low cardinality or hot values (e.g., NULL, status='Active'), most rows hash to the same partition → one thread does most work while others idle (CXPACKET waits). Fix: (1) filter out NULLs before the join, (2) pre-aggregate to reduce skew, (3) use OPTION(HASH GROUP, MAXDOP 1) for known-skewed joins, (4) consider merge join as alternative. SQL Server 2019 adaptive joins can switch from hash to nested loop at runtime but don't fix skew.
