1452	832	1400	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Exchange operators (Parallelism: Gather Streams, Repartition Streams, Distribute Streams) are the glue of parallel plans. Each exchange has: (1) buffer allocation overhead, (2) synchronization points where threads must coordinate, (3) data serialization/deserialization. Plans with 5+ exchanges may spend more time in coordination than computation. CXSYNC_PORT (SQL 2019+) specifically tracks exchange synchronization. Fix: (1) simplify query to reduce exchange count, (2) use MAXDOP 1 for queries with excessive exchanges, (3) break complex queries into simpler steps with temp tables to control parallelism boundaries.
