1507	856	1455	2	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Silent firewall drops (no TCP RST, just black-hole) are harder to detect from the server side because the connection attempt may never reach SQL Server. What is observable: (1) increased login rate from clients retrying, (2) connectivity ring buffer entries, (3) error log login failures. The RING_BUFFER_CONNECTIVITY DMV captures low-level connection events including timeouts. Fix: audit recent firewall/ACL changes, check Windows Firewall rules (netsh advfirewall), verify SQL Server Browser service accessibility on UDP 1434, and ensure the SQL Server port (typically 1433) is open for all expected client subnets.
