1527	866	1475	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Scalar UDFs in SQL Server (pre-2019) are executed once per row, prevent parallelism, and hide their true cost from the optimizer (estimated at 0 I/O). A scalar UDF called on 1M rows effectively runs 1M separate queries. SQL Server 2019+ introduced Scalar UDF Inlining (TSQL_SCALAR_UDF_INLINING) that can automatically inline eligible functions. MSTVFs always use a fixed cardinality estimate of 1 (pre-2017) or 100 (2017+), leading to bad plans. Fix: (1) rewrite as inline table-valued functions (iTVFs), (2) enable scalar UDF inlining (SQL 2019+), (3) move logic into the query directly, (4) use CROSS APPLY with an iTVF instead.
