1531	868	1479	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Lock contention wastes CPU in several ways: (1) lock manager overhead for acquiring/releasing millions of locks, (2) spinlock contention on internal lock hash buckets (LOCK_HASH), (3) lock escalation from row/page to table locks blocking concurrent access, (4) blocked sessions accumulating and retrying. Fix: (1) reduce transaction scope and duration, (2) use READ COMMITTED SNAPSHOT ISOLATION (RCSI) to eliminate reader-writer blocking, (3) optimize queries to reduce lock duration, (4) disable lock escalation on hot tables (ALTER TABLE SET LOCK_ESCALATION = DISABLE), (5) ensure proper indexing to minimize rows locked.
