1536	870	1484	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Sort and hash spills occur when the optimizer underestimates the memory needed for an operation. The total_spills column in sys.dm_exec_query_stats (SQL 2017+) tracks spill counts directly. Spills write intermediate data to tempdb, which is I/O-bound and much slower than memory. Common causes: (1) stale statistics causing cardinality underestimation, (2) too many concurrent memory-intensive queries competing for workspace memory, (3) Resource Governor memory limits. Fix: (1) update statistics for accurate cardinality estimates, (2) use OPTION (MIN_GRANT_PERCENT = N) to request more memory, (3) increase max server memory, (4) enable adaptive memory grants (SQL 2017+ batch mode, SQL 2019+ row mode).
