1541	872	1489	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Index fragmentation in SQL Server means leaf pages are not in logical order, causing range scans to perform random I/O instead of sequential I/O. Impact depends on storage: SSDs are less affected than HDDs, but buffer pool waste (partially-filled pages) affects all storage types. Thresholds: <5% ignore, 5-30% reorganize (ALTER INDEX REORGANIZE — online, minimal logging), >30% rebuild (ALTER INDEX REBUILD — more thorough, optionally online in Enterprise). Schedule maintenance windows or use Ola Hallengren's IndexOptimize. Note: fragmentation of small indexes (<1000 pages) has negligible impact — focus on large indexes.
