1548	875	1496	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Inefficient transaction handling in SQL Server manifests as: (1) Auto-commit overhead — each individual INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE in implicit transaction mode flushes the log, costing ~2ms per operation. Batch 1000 inserts: auto-commit = 1000 log flushes (~2 seconds), explicit transaction = 1 log flush (~2ms). (2) Long-running transactions — hold locks for minutes/hours, block checkpoint from advancing (log_reuse_wait = ACTIVE_TRANSACTION), prevent ghost cleanup, bloat version store. (3) Excessive rollbacks — wasted CPU on undo operations. Fix: (1) batch operations into explicit transactions (BEGIN TRAN / COMMIT), (2) keep transactions as short as possible, (3) never leave transactions open waiting for user input, (4) use SET XACT_ABORT ON to auto-rollback on errors.
