1573	887	1521	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Cache line bouncing occurs on multi-socket NUMA systems when the log buffer structures are allocated on one NUMA node but accessed by threads on other nodes. Each cross-node access requires cache coherency protocol (MESI), adding latency. SQL Server 2016+ improved log pool NUMA awareness. Fix: (1) ensure SQL Server NUMA affinity is configured correctly, (2) consider soft-NUMA configuration, (3) use trace flag 8048 (convert CMEMTHREAD to per-NUMA partitions). Lower confidence because spinlock stats don't directly attribute to NUMA bouncing — correlation requires hardware performance counters.
