1631	914	1578	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Parallel DML in SQL Server is only supported for INSERT...SELECT (since SQL Server 2016) and, in limited scenarios, UPDATE/DELETE with partitioned tables. The overhead comes from: (1) each parallel thread must acquire locks independently — hot pages create contention, (2) log records from all threads must serialize through the log buffer, (3) index maintenance on secondary indexes creates additional contention points. For INSERT...SELECT into heap: parallel insert is efficient. For INSERT into clustered index with identity: last-page contention negates parallelism. Fix: (1) use TABLOCK hint for minimal logging and reduced locking, (2) MAXDOP 1 for inserts into narrow tables or tables with many indexes, (3) batch large DML into smaller chunks.
