1640	917	1587	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Parallel query startup in SQL Server: (1) allocate DOP worker threads from thread pool, (2) initialize exchange buffers (CXMEM memory), (3) create exchange iterator state for each thread, (4) synchronize thread start via exchange open barriers. This costs ~0.5-2ms per execution even for trivial parallel plans. For a query that runs in 10ms with DOP=1, DOP=8 startup alone adds ~2ms overhead before any work begins. With 1000 executions/sec: 2 seconds of pure startup overhead per second. Fix: (1) raise cost threshold for parallelism to 25-50 to exclude short queries, (2) OPTION(MAXDOP 1) on known-short queries, (3) use query store hints. THREADPOOL waits indicate worker exhaustion from too many parallel queries.
