1643	918	1590	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	CPU cache efficiency degrades with parallelism because: (1) each thread has its own L1/L2 cache — spreading a working set across 8 cores means 8 separate cold caches, (2) parallel scan threads access different page ranges, preventing cache sharing, (3) on NUMA systems, threads on remote nodes pay 2-3x memory latency for non-local pages. For queries with small working sets (fits in L2/L3): serial execution keeps data hot in one cache hierarchy. Parallelism only helps when the working set is too large for one core's cache and the work is CPU-bound. Fix: (1) reduce DOP for lookup-heavy queries (index seeks with key lookups), (2) keep MAXDOP within one NUMA node, (3) MAXDOP 1 for queries where total CPU per execution < 10ms. Step 3 on_no_match is confirmed because even single-NUMA systems lose L1/L2 locality.
