1692	938	1639	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Page Life Expectancy (PLE) is the primary indicator for buffer pool pressure in SQL Server. The traditional threshold of 300 seconds was for servers with small memory; for large servers, use (max_server_memory_GB / 4) * 300. Free list stalls mean a query needed a buffer page but none were free — the lazy writer couldn't evict fast enough. High page_reads_sec with low PLE confirms constant cycling through the buffer pool. Fix: increase max server memory, add RAM, or optimize queries/indexes to reduce the working set. Consider Resource Governor memory pools for multi-database environments.
