1649	920	1596	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Auto-update thresholds: (1) Legacy (pre-2016 or compat < 130): 500 + 20% of rows — for a 10M row table, 2M modifications needed. (2) Dynamic (2016+ with compat >= 130 or TF 2371): approximately sqrt(1000 * rows) — for 10M rows, ~100K modifications. Even the dynamic threshold may be too high for rapidly changing distributions. For tables where data distribution shifts significantly with small modification counts (e.g., date-partitioned tables, status columns), consider: (1) scheduled UPDATE STATISTICS jobs, (2) sp_updatestats after ETL loads, (3) norecompute on specific stats with manual refresh. The modification_counter in dm_db_stats_properties shows accumulated changes since last update.
