1652	921	1599	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	After bulk operations (BCP, BULK INSERT, INSERT...SELECT, MERGE, partition switching), statistics may not auto-update until the modification threshold is reached. For very large tables with dynamic threshold, even 30% data change may not trigger auto-update. Critical: (1) BULK INSERT with TABLOCK uses minimal logging — fast but doesn't update stats, (2) partition switches (ALTER TABLE...SWITCH) move data without modifying stats on target, (3) MERGE with large source can modify most of the table. Best practice: always run UPDATE STATISTICS immediately after bulk operations. Use FULLSCAN for critical tables, or a percentage for very large tables. Check sp.rows vs p.rows to detect discrepancy.
