1654	922	1601	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Filtered statistics/indexes only cover a subset of rows (e.g., WHERE status = 'Active'). The auto-update threshold counts modifications against the entire table, not the filtered subset. For a 10M row table with 100K active rows: filtered stats may need 500 + 20K modifications to trigger update, but 10K changes to the 'Active' subset (10% of filtered rows) already makes the histogram stale. SQL Server tracks modification_counter for filtered stats separately starting in 2016, but the threshold is still based on filtered row count. Fix: (1) schedule UPDATE STATISTICS on filtered stats more frequently, (2) create maintenance jobs targeting filtered indexes specifically, (3) use sp_updatestats which updates all statistics including filtered.
