1656	923	1603	1	next	\N	next	\N	When AUTO_CREATE_STATISTICS is ON (default), SQL Server creates single-column statistics on first query use. But: (1) if disabled, no statistics are ever auto-created, (2) auto-creation only happens for columns used in WHERE/JOIN/GROUP BY — columns used only in SELECT don't get stats, (3) columns added via ALTER TABLE after initial schema setup may not have statistics until a query needs them, (4) the first query to trigger auto-creation pays the compilation cost. Missing statistics cause the optimizer to use: 30% selectivity for equality predicates, 30% for range predicates, geometric mean for AND conditions. Fix: (1) enable AUTO_CREATE_STATISTICS, (2) run CREATE STATISTICS manually for new columns, (3) check query plans for MissingStatistics element in XML.
