1659	924	1606	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	SQL Server auto statistics sampling: for tables < 8MB, FULLSCAN; for larger tables, a dynamic percentage that decreases as table size grows (1M rows: ~30%, 10M rows: ~10%, 100M rows: ~3%). A histogram has max 200 steps regardless of sample size. Low sampling can miss: (1) data skew on infrequent values, (2) correlation between columns, (3) non-uniform distribution within histogram steps. Critical for: columns with many distinct values, columns with skewed distribution (80/20 patterns), foreign keys to large dimension tables. Fix: (1) UPDATE STATISTICS WITH FULLSCAN for critical tables, (2) UPDATE STATISTICS WITH SAMPLE 50 PERCENT for very large tables, (3) sp_updatestats uses default sampling. The PERSIST_SAMPLE_PERCENT option (2016 SP1+) remembers the sample rate for future auto-updates.
