1667	928	1614	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	SQL Server incremental statistics (2014+): per-partition statistics that can be updated individually without rescanning the entire table. Without incremental stats: (1) UPDATE STATISTICS scans all partitions even if only one changed, (2) auto-update threshold is based on total table modifications, so changes concentrated in one partition may not trigger update. With incremental stats: (1) each partition has its own histogram and modification counter, (2) UPDATE STATISTICS only rescans modified partitions, (3) per-partition auto-update thresholds. Prerequisites: (1) database compatibility level >= 120, (2) statistics created with INCREMENTAL = ON, (3) AUTO_CREATE_STATS_INCREMENTAL_ON database option. Use sys.dm_db_incremental_stats_properties to view per-partition stats. Fix: CREATE STATISTICS WITH INCREMENTAL = ON, or ALTER DATABASE SET AUTO_CREATE_STATISTICS_INCREMENTAL ON.
