1669	929	1616	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Data cleansing operations (normalizing addresses, standardizing codes, fixing NULLs, trimming strings) change column value distributions without changing row counts. Statistics modification_counter tracks these as updates, but the auto-update threshold may not trigger if: (1) changes are spread across many columns, (2) total modifications per column stay below threshold. The histogram remains based on old value distribution. Example: cleansing a status column from 50 values to 5 — old histogram has 50 steps with old frequencies, queries on new values get wrong estimates. Fix: (1) UPDATE STATISTICS WITH FULLSCAN immediately after data cleansing, (2) for large tables, UPDATE STATISTICS on specific cleansed columns, (3) add cleansing jobs to ETL pipelines with post-step stats refresh.
