1672	930	1619	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	SQL Server incremental statistics (2014+) store per-partition statistics that can be individually updated. Without incremental: UPDATE STATISTICS scans the entire table regardless of which partition changed. For a 100-partition, 1B-row table: (1) non-incremental UPDATE STATISTICS may take 30+ minutes, (2) incremental UPDATE STATISTICS on one partition takes seconds, (3) auto-update threshold is per-partition (modification threshold against partition row count, not total). Requirements: (1) compat level >= 120, (2) create with INCREMENTAL = ON, (3) cannot use filtered statistics with incremental. Fix: (1) ALTER DATABASE SET AUTO_CREATE_STATISTICS_INCREMENTAL ON, (2) recreate existing statistics with INCREMENTAL = ON: DROP STATISTICS / CREATE STATISTICS WITH INCREMENTAL = ON, FULLSCAN. This is a very SQL Server-native feature that directly addresses the partition statistics problem.
