1681	933	1628	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	The density vector (accessible via DBCC SHOW_STATISTICS WITH DENSITY_VECTOR) stores 1/distinct_count for each column prefix combination in the statistics. The optimizer uses density for: (1) equality predicates on non-histogram columns (columns 2+ in multi-column stats), (2) GROUP BY cardinality estimation, (3) DISTINCT estimation, (4) join cardinality when no histogram step matches. When data changes: new values added (density decreases), values consolidated (density increases), but the stats density remains at the old value. This is especially impactful for: (1) growing dimension tables (new product categories, new customers), (2) data consolidation (merging duplicate records), (3) temporal data where distinct dates/months grow over time. Fix: (1) UPDATE STATISTICS WITH FULLSCAN for accurate density, (2) schedule regular stats maintenance for tables with evolving distinct value counts, (3) use PERSIST_SAMPLE_PERCENT to ensure consistent sampling on auto-update.
