1695	939	1642	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	The checkpoint coordinator in SQL Server manages the flushing of dirty pages to disk. With automatic checkpoint, the coordinator triggers based on the recovery interval setting. With indirect checkpoint, it runs continuously. A bottleneck occurs when the rate of dirty pages exceeds the checkpoint's ability to flush them. CHKPT wait type indicates threads waiting for checkpoint completion. CHECKPOINT_QUEUE indicates pending checkpoint requests. If the checkpoint is always running but dirty pages keep growing, the I/O subsystem cannot sustain the write rate. Fix: faster storage, separate data files across I/O paths, increase target_recovery_time to reduce checkpoint aggressiveness.
