1713	947	1660	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	PFS (Page Free Space) pages track free space on each page in a data file. Page 1 of each data file is the first PFS page. Every allocation or deallocation of a page requires updating the PFS page, acquiring an UP latch. With few tempdb files, all allocations contend on the same PFS pages. The wait_resource format is 'database_id:file_id:page_id' — '2:1:1' means tempdb, file 1, PFS page. Each additional tempdb file adds another PFS page, distributing contention. SQL Server 2019 introduced PFS concurrency optimization (enabled by default) that reduces this contention. Fix: add more tempdb data files, upgrade to SQL Server 2019+ for built-in PFS optimization, or enable TF 3427 (pre-2019).
