1715	948	1662	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	GAM (Global Allocation Map) pages track which extents (8 contiguous pages = 64KB) are allocated. Page 2 of each data file is the first GAM page. Every uniform extent allocation must update the GAM page. In tempdb with heavy temp table and worktable creation, GAM contention is common when there are too few data files. Each additional tempdb file adds another GAM page, distributing allocation activity. The wait_resource '2:1:2' means tempdb, file 1, GAM page. Fix: add tempdb data files (1 per CPU up to 8), enable TF 1118 (uniform extent allocation, default in SQL 2016+). TF 1118 helps because it avoids mixed extent allocation which touches both GAM and SGAM.
