1739	957	1686	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	When SQL Server is under memory pressure, the query memory grant system reduces grants below the ideal level. Queries that receive reduced grants are more likely to spill sort, hash join, and hash aggregate operations to tempdb. This creates a cascading effect: memory pressure → reduced grants → spills to tempdb → increased tempdb I/O → further performance degradation. Fixes: (1) increase max server memory setting, (2) reduce memory consumers (plan cache bloat, MEMORYCLERK_SQLBUFFERPOOL), (3) optimize queries to require less memory, (4) enable Resource Governor to protect critical workloads.
