1742	958	853	1	next	\N	next	\N	SORT_IN_TEMPDB=ON directs the intermediate sort runs for index creation/rebuild to tempdb instead of the target database's filegroup. This is beneficial when tempdb is on faster storage or to avoid fragmenting the target filegroup, but harmful when tempdb is already under contention. The sort data can be very large — for a 10 GB table, the sort intermediate results can be 10+ GB. Fix: (1) schedule index rebuilds during low activity, (2) ensure tempdb is on fast dedicated storage, (3) consider SORT_IN_TEMPDB=OFF if target filegroup has headroom, (4) use ONLINE=ON with RESUMABLE for large indexes.
