1957	1053	1901	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Foreign key constraint validation in SQL Server requires a shared lock check on the referenced (parent) table for INSERT/UPDATE on the child, and a scan of the child table for DELETE/UPDATE on the parent key. Without an index on the FK column in the child table, the child scan is a table scan with shared locks on every row. This is the most common FK-related locking issue. Fix: (1) create an index on the FK column in the child table (most important), (2) use NOCHECK constraint during bulk operations then re-enable with CHECK, (3) consider CASCADE DELETE/UPDATE to batch the operation. is_not_trusted=1 means the FK was re-enabled with NOCHECK — the optimizer cannot use it for join elimination.
