2087	1105	2030	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	IMPLICIT_TRANSACTIONS (SET IMPLICIT_TRANSACTIONS ON or ANSI_DEFAULTS) causes SQL Server to automatically begin a transaction on the first DML/DDL statement. The transaction remains open until the application explicitly issues COMMIT or ROLLBACK. Many applications (especially those ported from Oracle or using ODBC/JDBC with auto-commit off) inadvertently leave implicit transactions open. This causes: (1) transaction log growth (log cannot truncate past the oldest open transaction), (2) lock accumulation (every statement's locks are held), (3) tempdb version store growth under RCSI. Fix: (1) ensure application explicitly commits after each logical unit of work, (2) set SET IMPLICIT_TRANSACTIONS OFF at session level, (3) configure the ODBC/JDBC driver to use auto-commit mode, (4) monitor with sys.dm_tran_active_transactions filtering for name = 'implicit_transaction'.
