2164	1141	2106	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Multiple sorts occur in queries with ORDER BY combined with GROUP BY (when the grouping and ordering columns differ), DISTINCT with ORDER BY, subqueries with their own ORDER BY, window functions with different PARTITION BY/ORDER BY clauses, and UNION (sort-based dedup) with ORDER BY. Each sort operator gets a memory reservation, and when sorts overlap in the pipeline (e.g., sort feeding into another sort), both need memory simultaneously. Fix: (1) add indexes that provide pre-sorted input, eliminating explicit sorts, (2) rewrite queries to unify sort requirements (same ORDER BY direction as GROUP BY), (3) break complex queries into steps using temp tables to separate sort operations, (4) for window functions, align PARTITION BY/ORDER BY clauses across windows to share a single sort.
