2176	1146	2118	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	The buffer cache hit ratio measures the percentage of page requests satisfied from the buffer pool vs disk. Values below 95% on an OLTP system indicate significant memory pressure. Page Life Expectancy (PLE) below 300 seconds (or below 300 * (buffer_pool_GB / 4) for larger instances) means pages are being evicted too quickly. Fix: (1) increase 'max server memory (MB)' via sp_configure if physical RAM is available, (2) add physical RAM to the server, (3) reduce memory consumers — query workspace memory (high grants), plan cache bloat, CLR memory, (4) optimize queries to reduce the working dataset (add indexes, reduce table scans), (5) enable lock pages in memory (LPIM) to prevent OS from paging out the buffer pool, (6) investigate if other applications are competing for RAM on the same server.
