2188	1150	2129	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Full table scans on large tables read every page into the buffer pool. For tables larger than the buffer pool, a single scan evicts all other cached pages. SQL Server's internal clock algorithm uses page reference counts for eviction — scan-accessed pages have low reference counts and are evicted quickly, but not before displacing useful pages. The Full Scans/sec counter from Access Methods tracks clustered index scans and heap scans. Target: < 1 full scan/sec per 1000 batch requests/sec. Fix: add appropriate indexes, rewrite queries to use seeks, or consider indexed views.
