2190	1151	2131	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Index fragmentation has two buffer pool impacts: (1) Logical fragmentation forces extra I/O for range scans (out-of-order pages can't use sequential readahead efficiently). (2) Low page density (avg_page_space_used_in_percent < 70%) means more pages are needed to hold the same data — wasting buffer pool. A 50% page density doubles the buffer pool footprint for that index. DBCC CHECKDB detects corruption; sys.dm_db_index_physical_stats detects fragmentation. Fix: ALTER INDEX REBUILD or REORGANIZE for fragmentation. Use Ola Hallengren's maintenance solution for automated scheduling.
