2216	1163	2157	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	SQL Server's auto-update statistics triggers at ~20% modification threshold (500 + 20% of rows). For large tables (1M+ rows), this means 200K+ modifications before stats refresh — the estimates can be badly wrong in the interim. Additionally, auto-update uses default sample rate which may miss data distribution changes. Fix: (1) UPDATE STATISTICS with FULLSCAN on critical tables, (2) enable TF 2371 for dynamic threshold (or use SQL 2016+ where it's default), (3) create a statistics maintenance job that runs more frequently than the auto threshold, (4) use incremental statistics for partitioned tables.
