2218	1164	2159	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Data skew is when some column values appear far more frequently than others (e.g., status='Active' has 95% of rows, other statuses have 1% each). The optimizer uses histogram step values for known constants but falls back to average density for parameters. With skewed data, the average density wildly underestimates popular values and overestimates rare ones. This causes: (1) popular values: memory grant too small → spill to tempdb, (2) rare values: memory grant too large → waste. dm_db_stats_histogram (SQL 2016+) exposes the histogram steps for analysis. Fix: create filtered statistics for skewed values, use OPTION(RECOMPILE) for parameter-sensitive queries, add multi-column statistics, consider Query Store forced plans for known-good plans.
