2345	1222	2283	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	SQL Server uses cooperative (non-preemptive) scheduling where worker threads voluntarily yield the scheduler. When a thread enters preemptive mode (for OS calls, COM interop, CLR, linked server OLEDB, backup I/O), it leaves the SQL OS scheduler and holds the worker until the external call completes. During this time, the worker cannot be reused. Common culprits: PREEMPTIVE_OS_WRITEFILEGATHER (file growth), PREEMPTIVE_OLEDBOPS (linked servers), PREEMPTIVE_COM_QUERYINTERFACE (COM objects), PREEMPTIVE_OS_AUTHENTICATIONOPS (AD authentication). Fix: pre-grow database files to avoid WRITEFILEGATHER, optimize linked server queries, cache authentication tokens, move CLR operations to background tasks.
