2900	1508	2836	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	RBAC in SQL Server means: (1) create custom database roles representing job functions (app_reader, app_writer, report_user), (2) grant permissions to roles, (3) add users to appropriate roles. Without RBAC, each user gets individual GRANT statements — this is unmanageable at scale, error-prone, and difficult to audit. Direct grants also make onboarding/offboarding expensive: every permission must be individually revoked. Fix: (1) create custom roles mapped to application functions, (2) migrate direct user grants to role grants (GRANT permission TO role; ALTER ROLE role ADD MEMBER user), (3) remove direct user grants (REVOKE), (4) document role definitions.
