2902	1509	2838	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Principle of least privilege means users should have only the minimum permissions required. In SQL Server, common violations: (1) application service accounts in sysadmin (should have only db_datareader/db_datawriter on their database), (2) developers in db_owner on production (should have read-only), (3) multiple DBAs in sysadmin when only 2-3 are needed. Step 2 on_no_match is confirmed because having >3 logins in high-privilege server roles (from step 1) is already a finding. Fix: (1) create custom roles with minimum required permissions, (2) remove db_owner and use granular permissions (GRANT SELECT, GRANT EXECUTE), (3) implement just-in-time access for elevated privileges.
