2909	1513	2845	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Multi-schema and cross-database applications create privilege complexity: the application needs SELECT on schema_a.orders AND schema_b.products AND [other_db].dbo.config. Instead of creating precise cross-database permissions, the common shortcut is: (1) enable cross-database ownership chaining (dangerous — allows implicit access), (2) grant db_owner on all databases, (3) add the login to sysadmin. Fix: (1) disable cross-database ownership chaining, (2) use module signing (EXECUTE AS, certificate-based) for cross-database access, (3) create per-database custom roles with minimum permissions, (4) consolidate related data into the same database where possible.
