2911	1514	2847	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Third-party vendors frequently require sysadmin in their documentation as a 'supported configuration' because it avoids support tickets about permission errors. The actual application typically only needs: (1) SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE on its schema, (2) EXECUTE on its stored procedures, (3) occasionally VIEW SERVER STATE for monitoring. Fix: (1) profile the vendor application's actual SQL statements using Extended Events, (2) create a custom role matching the actual permission usage, (3) test the application with the custom role in a non-production environment, (4) negotiate with the vendor — many will provide a minimum permissions list on request. Step 2 on_no_match is confirmed because having vendor apps with sysadmin (from step 1) is itself the finding.
