3328	1740	3260	1	confirmed	\N	ruled_out	\N	Operational automation (backup verification, disk space checks, file management, log cycling) commonly uses xp_cmdshell in SQL Agent jobs because it was the simplest way to interact with the OS from T-SQL. Common patterns: xp_cmdshell 'del /q /f ...', xp_fileexist for backup verification, xp_dirtree for directory listings, xp_fixeddrives for disk space monitoring, xp_readerrorlog for log parsing. Fix: replace with SQL Agent CmdExec subsystem steps (no xp_cmdshell needed), PowerShell job steps, SSIS packages, or CLR stored procedures. SQL Agent's CmdExec and PowerShell subsystems provide the same OS interaction without xp_cmdshell.
