3350	1750	3282	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	SQL Server binds to all interfaces (0.0.0.0) by default via SQL Server Configuration Manager's TCP/IP protocol settings. Unlike PostgreSQL's listen_addresses or MySQL's bind-address, SQL Server's per-IP configuration is done in Configuration Manager (not via T-SQL). Each IP address can be individually enabled/disabled with specific ports. Step 2 on_no_match is still confirmed because even with a single interface, listening on 0.0.0.0 means ANY future network adapter added to the host will automatically be exposed. Fix: in SQL Server Configuration Manager > SQL Server Network Configuration > Protocols > TCP/IP > IP Addresses: disable 'IP All', enable only specific required IP addresses. Requires SQL Server service restart.
