3415	1777	3345	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	Step 1 checks for server-level audit groups that capture all data access. SCHEMA_OBJECT_ACCESS_GROUP is especially broad — it logs every SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE on any schema object. Step 2 checks database-level specs for unrestricted SELECT auditing (major_id = 0 means all objects). Step 2 on_no_match is still 'confirmed' because step 1 already matched server-level broad auditing. The fix is to scope auditing to specific tables containing sensitive data rather than auditing everything. Consider also enabling audit log encryption and strict access controls on audit files.
