3419	1779	3349	1	next	\N	ruled_out	\N	SQL Server generates mini dumps, full dumps, or filtered dumps on internal errors (stack dumps, access violations, assertions). Full dumps contain complete process memory including buffer pool pages, plan cache entries, and in-flight query data — any PII being processed at crash time is in the dump. Dump files are written to the SQL Server LOG directory and are accessible to anyone with OS read permissions. The default trace (enabled by default) writes .trc files with event data. Neither dump files nor default trace files are encrypted.
