3423	1781	3353	1	next	\N	next	\N	SQL Trace (the engine behind SQL Server Profiler) is deprecated since SQL Server 2012 in favor of Extended Events, but traces left running from debugging sessions are common. The default trace (id=1, is_default=1) is always running and captures a subset of events. Non-default traces (is_default=0, status=1) are typically left behind by developers or DBAs who ran Profiler and forgot to stop it. Trace files (.trc) are plain binary files readable with fn_trace_gettable — anyone with OS read access can extract query text. Step 2 specifically checks for statement-level events with TextData capture.
